From 24b98f63836115f9c0351ea940aa9a2faf147e44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:01:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.9.9c: all-bands Professional - drop Hide SSID + AP
 Isolation (SDN-governed)

Metal feedback (v1.9.9b): "Hide SSID" toggled off/on but the main SSID never
hid. Root cause: this is a MULTILAN_MWL/SDN build - the user's main SSID is an
SDN MAINFH profile, so the radio-level wlN_closed / wlN_ap_isolate only affect
the internal primary/backhaul BSS, not the SSID clients join. Stock hides both
on this hardware (class .mainBH under isSupport("sdn_mainfh"), Advanced_WAdvanced
L834); the all-bands page surfaced them ungated - a control that didn't do what
it said.

Fix: remove Hide SSID + AP Isolation from Reaper_WiFiPro.asp (29 rows now).
Footer note (RWFP_12) updated: main-network SSID visibility + client isolation
are set on the General Wireless and Network pages, where the real SSID lives.
Everything else on the page was metal-confirmed working and is unchanged.

i18n: RWFP_12 re-seeded (EN) in all 25 dicts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
